<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-toolbar</code></td><td>block</td><td>a wrapping row with padding and a line below</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-toolbar__search</code></td><td>element</td><td>grows from 14rem, at most 22rem (put it on the input group)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-toolbar__spacer</code></td><td>element</td><td>pushes what follows to the end</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-toolbar .dnf-select</code></td><td>-</td><td><code>width: auto</code>, at least 9rem - as tall as the search field</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-collection-bar</code></td><td>block</td><td><code>position: relative</code>; its <code>&gt; .dnf-bulk-bar</code> covers the toolbar (absolute, <code>inset: 0</code>), so nothing below moves; at 64rem and below it wraps and replaces the toolbar</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-bulk-bar</code></td><td>block</td><td>an opaque primary-tinted row, medium weight, a primary-tinted line below</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-bulk-bar__count</code></td><td>element</td><td>the "3 selected" text; no wrap</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-bulk-bar .dnf-select</code></td><td>-</td><td><code>width: auto</code>, at most 16rem</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>nothing selected</td><td><code>.dnf-bulk-bar[hidden]</code></td><td>the toolbar shows</td></tr>
        <tr><td>items selected</td><td><code>.dnf-bulk-bar</code> without <code>hidden</code></td><td>the bulk bar covers the toolbar; <code>dnf.js</code> toggles <code>hidden</code> and writes "N selected" into <code>[data-bulk-count]</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>The toolbar has no tag helper: the classes above are its API. The controls in it work through the collection hooks of
    <code>dnf.js</code> on an ancestor with <code>data-collection</code> (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/behaviours">Behaviours</a>):</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>On</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data-collection-search</code></td><td>the search input</td><td>keeps the items whose <code>data-search</code> (else their text) contains the query, ignoring case</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-collection-filter="key"</code></td><td>a <code>&lt;select&gt;</code></td><td>keeps the items whose <code>data-key</code> has the selected value among its words; an empty value is no filter</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-collection-filter="key"</code> + <code>data-value</code></td><td>buttons (a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/segmented">segmented</a> control)</td><td>the same as exclusive buttons: the clicked one gets <code>aria-pressed="true"</code>, the others <code>"false"</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-collection-count</code></td><td>any text element</td><td>"N total", or "X of N" while filtered</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-bulk-bar</code></td><td>the bulk bar</td><td>shown while at least one <code>[data-select-item]</code> is checked</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-bulk-count</code></td><td>the count</td><td>"N selected"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-bulk-clear</code></td><td>a button</td><td>unchecks every item</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Search, filter and page-size changes go back to page 1. Item checkboxes can post with a bulk form elsewhere on the
    page through <code>form="…"</code>.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Label every control - <code>aria-label</code> when there is no visible label ("Search pages", "Status").</li>
    <li>Give a segmented filter a group name: <code>role="group"</code> and <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
    <li>The bulk bar's count is plain text; <code>aria-live="polite"</code> on it announces selection changes.</li>
    <li>Selection needs JavaScript: keep every bulk action available on each item too (its row menu).</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do hide a toolbar that only drives client-side filtering until <code>dnf.js</code> runs: <code>hidden data-js-only</code>.</li>
    <li>Do keep search first, filters next, actions last after the spacer.</li>
    <li>Don't repeat the screen's primary action in the toolbar when the page header already has it.</li>
    <li>Don't put destructive bulk actions without a confirmation in the bulk bar.</li>
</ul>
